417] [17592186562319 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562319 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562319 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562319 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562319 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186561603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562319 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "91ed0fd0-f788-5c51-8051-a72f994211f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562324 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562324 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562324 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562324 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561921 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562324 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562324 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562324 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562324 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186561711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562324 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "96e90e80-750f-5c33-af90-c6f2fdc5beb0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562340 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562340 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562340 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186561958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562340 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562055 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562340 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562340 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562340 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562340 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186561826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562340 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bb13cd8f-4bfe-5cf0-87bd-31c8b6751181" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562391 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562391 #edb/ref 1069 "q-185132" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562391 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562391 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the missing number?\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\times \\,45%=18$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562391 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0548a4d1-2f13-56af-b405-5e95b48898dc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562391 #edb/ref 1074 "The part is $18,$ the percentage is $45%,$ and we need to find the whole.\n\nTo do this, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{whole}=\\text{part}÷\\text{percentage}\n$$\n\nBefore we can substitute our numbers into the formula, we need to express $45%$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{45}{100}=\\frac{45÷5}{100÷5}=\\frac{9}{20}\n$$\n\nWe can now substitute our numbers into the formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{whole} & =18÷45% \\\\  & =18÷\\frac{9}{20} \\\\  & =18\\times \\frac{20}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{9}\\times 20 \\\\  & =2\\times 20 \\\\  & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $40.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562396 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562396 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562396 #edb/ref 1069 "q-171693" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562396 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562396 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-u+v=-1 \\\\ 3u+3v=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(u,v)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(u,v)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562396 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c604a3f-ba93-531d-b858-55cd303f28fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562396 #edb/ref 1074 "We will isolate a variable in one of the equations and then substitute it into the other equation. It doesn't matter which equation we pick first, so we choose the easiest one. In this case, the first equation looks like the easiest.\n\nUsing the first equation, we can isolate $v$ by adding $u$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\nv=u-1\n$$\n\nSo, we replace $v$ with $u-1$ in the second equation and solve for $u:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3u+3v & =5 \\\\ 3u+3(u-1) & =5 \\\\ 3u+3u-3 & =5 \\\\ 6u & =8 \\\\ u & =\\frac{8}{6} \\\\ u & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we now substitute $u=\\frac{4}{3}$ into $v=u-1,$ then we can find the value of $v:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u-1 \\\\ v & =\\frac{4}{3}-1 \\\\ v & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $u=\\frac{4}{3},\\,v=\\frac{1}{3},$ which can be expressed as $(\\frac{4}{3},\\frac{1}{3}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562415 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562415 #edb/ref 1069 "q-120503" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562415 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562415 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/fa/fa455c343dc5e6fea5fe9fee9b22b0cfa0ef098c1fb7ae8ea361d9db78e5cc1b.png)\n\nWhat is a correct congruence statement for the pentagons shown in the diagram above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562415 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2eafcea3-29cb-5583-a92c-83cb3e6d71ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562415 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that $∠A≅∠B≅∠C.$ \n\nLet's determine the vertices in the second pentagon that correspond to $A.$ First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =QR \\\\ EA & =RS \\\\ ∠A & ≅∠R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- vertex $A$ corresponds to vertex $R.$\n\nSimilarly, for vertices in the second pentagon that correspond to $C.$ First, notice the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =PQ \\\\ CD & =PT \\\\ ∠C & ≅∠P\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- vertex $C$ corresponds to vertex $P,$\n\n- consequently, vertex $B$ corresponds to vertex $Q.$\n\nAs for the other two vertices, notice we have two more pairs of congruent angles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∠D & ≅∠T \\\\ ∠E & ≅∠S.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have one more pair of congruent sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DE & =TS.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n- vertex $D$ corresponds to vertex $T,$\n\n- vertex $E$ corresponds to vertex $S.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that a correct congruence statement is\n\n$$\nABCDE≅RQPTS.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562417 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562309 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562417 #edb/ref 1069 "q-68235" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562417 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562417 #edb/ref 1071 "The relationship between the number of cars $n$ Steve washes in $t$ hours is shown in the following table:\n\n| Hours  ($t$) | Cars ($n$) |\n| --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $4$ |\n| $3$ | $12$ |\n| $5$ | $20$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. There is **not** a proportional relationship between $n$ and $t.$\n\nII. The constant of proportionality is $4.$\n\nIII. There is a proportional relationship between $n$ and $t.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562417 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "306ea2e9-4291-50e8-bb35-b93734ac5dfd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562417 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's add a new column to our table and compute the ratio of cars per hour for each row.     \n\n| Hours ($t$) | Cars ($n$) | Cars / Hours |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $4$ | $4$ |\n| $3$ | $12$ | $4$ |\n| $5$ | $20$ | $4$ |\n\nThe ratio of cars per hour is the same for each row. Therefore, there is a proportional relationship between $n$ and $t.$ The constant of proportionality is $4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III  only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562456 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562220 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562456 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75780" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562456 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562456 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/36/36a99d1e792635936b3321144e89782e02cec2442a3cf2082939b3e78cdb69f4.png)\n\nWhat is the circumference of a circle with a radius of $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi }?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562456 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "894f2b41-1597-5b67-ba7a-303a5bd60b9b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562456 #edb/ref 1074 "We use the formula $C=2\\pi r$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =2\\pi r \\\\  & =2\\pi \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562467 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562319 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562467 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119313" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562467 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562467 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/10/1073020fe8576784ed24601864f8546a72b426d8f02670b1a8c13923dc16e35f.png)\n\nThe perimeter of the triangle above is $30+15\\sqrt{2}.$ Find the measure of the hypotenuse." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562467 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9c716292-5467-511e-9d08-e7988cf3fd66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562467 #edb/ref 1074 "Because the triangle is isosceles, the legs must have the same length. Let $a$ be the length of each leg. So, we have\n\n$$\nAB=BC=a.\n$$\n\nMoreover, because the triangle is a *right* isosceles triangle, the hypotenuse must be equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg. Therefore,\n\n$$\nAC=AB\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=a\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the perimeter is $p=30+15\\sqrt{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+AC \\\\ 30+15\\sqrt{2} & =a+a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 30+15\\sqrt{2} & =2a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 15(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =a(2+\\sqrt{2}) \\\\ 15\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} & =a\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} \\\\ 15 & =a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of each leg is $a=15,$ and the length of the hypotenuse is\n\n$$\nAC=a\\sqrt{2}=15\\sqrt{2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562474 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562340 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562474 #edb/ref 1069 "q-318218" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562474 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562474 #edb/ref 1071 "A startup launched its website with $25$ initial visitors. An exponential model estimates that at the end of each day after launch, the number of visitors increased by $300%$ of the number of visitors at the end of the previous day.\n\nAccording to this model, how many visitors are there estimated to be after $3$ days?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562474 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ae3f3bc6-d6de-5132-b72c-58e7d4ad1247" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562474 #edb/ref 1074 "The number of visitors $V(t)$ grows exponentially with a growth rate of $300%.$\n\nLet's write down what we know:\n\n- $a=25$ is the total number of visitors initially\n\n- $r=3.0$ is the growth rate ($300%$ expressed as a decimal)\n\n- $t=$ the time (in days) after launch\n\nThe formula for exponential growth is\n\n$$\nV=a(1+r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $V(t)$ is\n\n$$\nV=25\\cdot (1+3.0)^{t}.\n$$\n\nSimplifying the above, we get\n\n$$\nV(t)=25\\cdot (4)^{t}.\n$$\n\nTo find the total number of visitors after $3$ days, we evaluate the above for $t=3:$\n\n$$\nV(3)=25\\cdot (4)^{3}=25\\cdot 64=1600\n$$\n\nTherefore, the estimated number of visitors after $3$ days is $1600.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562486 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562291 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562486 #edb/ref 1069 "q-33475" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562486 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562486 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify $\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{{s}^{2}}}\\,$ given that $s>0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562486 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ba7dd967-8709-5d76-b1fe-877b52dd2156" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562486 #edb/ref 1074 "The square root of a squared quantity can be simplified using absolute value.\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{{x}^{2}}=|x|\n$$\n\nIn our case, we can simplify the given expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{49}{{s}^{2}}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{s}\\cdot \\frac{7}{s}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{(\\frac{7}{s})}^{2}} & = \\\\ |\\frac{7}{s}| & = \\\\ \\frac{|7|}{|s|} & = \\\\ \\frac{7}{|s|} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are told that $s>0,$ and we know that the absolute value of any positive number is just itself, so we have $|s|=s.$ Therefore, our final answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{|s|}=\\frac{7}{s}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562494 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186562324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562494 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158615" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562494 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562494 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/a3/a3e86e25d02f4bf51f0f1fcad5f3be92dc87141b0ae1bf775eb3b9ec9d05aa28.png)\n\nGiven that $r$, $s$ and $t$ in the above diagram are parallel, find $m∠1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562494 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c9000a57-600a-5a19-a505-3e46af6f2315" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562494 #edb/ref 1074 "Consider $∠2$ and $∠3$ in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/44/44552b4c1624cd049769bf672d510c33f5cfdb53a8726ada5e0ed4cafea11b64.png)\n\nNote that $∠2$ and the angle whose measure is ${80}^{∘}$ are corresponding angles formed by the same transversal. Therefore, \n\n$$\nm∠2={80}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, note that $∠3$ and the angle whose measure is ${50}^{∘}$ are corresponding angles formed by the same transversal. Therefore, \n\n$$\nm∠3={50}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these measures to our diagram:\n\n![](images/46/4672d1aa0d64c5af11c85bb90f834a440eb53a4b9e490ce1b0cb22b5306f4f27.png)\n\nThe angles $∠1$, $∠2,$ and $∠3$ combined give a straight angle. So, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠1+m∠2+m∠3 & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠1+{80}^{∘}+{50}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠1+{130}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠1 & ={50}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562536 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186562541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562536 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4d3ec7d5-7957-5b77-8fcf-b7512ec71cc0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562536 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186562467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562538 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186562539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562538 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5212f0b9-a952-5ee7-b9dd-50ff53ec2bdf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562538 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186562474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562539 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186562551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562539 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "527b51e5-9e93-5aef-9912-015e4e655b04" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562539 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186562417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562541 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186562576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562541 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "575beec5-5a8d-5a79-932a-7aaa08ca4e91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562541 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186562486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562551 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186562536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562551 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7b1b3f97-d3de-5805-bab4-a25987ed070b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562551 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186562415 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562560 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186562538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562560 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9cdc12b6-2e47-5c72-bfe3-925ee2a1fefd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562560 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186562494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562566 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186562570 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562566 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b36c5d6b-e0af-5923-a241-f7bdc31fb6d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562566 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186562396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562570 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c51c6274-c6ab-5801-866e-5c82fde42940" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562570 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186562456 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562576 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186562566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562576 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d090bee6-5a64-5716-b2b7-162f4c278768" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186562576 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 175